  "chain": "inadequate procedural guidance re: fuse holder tightness [cause D] -> fuse holder works loose over time -> loose fuse holder connection (parallel: unrelated loose lead found/tightened) -> loss of power to HPCI flow controller -> HPCI inoperable (~15h50m) [backups RCIC, ADS operable]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two distinct connection issues were found: an initially-discovered loose lead (tightened, restored power at 20:23, but later determined it could not have caused the original loss of power) and a separately-discovered loose fuse holder connection (the actual root cause, per cause code D). Both are modeled as parallel FailureModes leading to loss of power, but only the fuse-holder issue is CAUSED_BY the cause node per the narrative's explicit attribution. RCIC and ADS are stated as having 'remained operable during this event' -> modeled as BACKED_UP_BY. Previous similar events are modeled as stub LERs keyed by their Event Notification numbers since no formal LER numbers were given in the narrative; EN-55780 was retracted but is still referenced as a previous similar event per the narrative."
